## 2. ANIMATION — full focus, the best (Alex: "animation pe full focus karo ... saab ekdum perfect banana h")

Use ALL of this (researched Nov 25, on top of §4/§4b/§4c Round 2 — the M3E table and one-scalar morph still stand):
- **One scalar spring drives width + height + radius + translation + scrim together.** Never separate width/height springs (they drift on interruption). Content is a HANDOVER at ~55% of morph, never a crossfade. C1 continuity via Animatable/spring() retargeting, never cancel-and-restart with tween.
- **Apple curve cubic-bezier(0.32, 0.72, 0, 1):** 70–80% of distance in first ~30% of time, long feather settle. Nothing starts slow.
- **Springs:** expand/collapse spring(dampingRatio = 0.75, stiffness = 400f) — one gentle overshoot, settles ~450–600 ms. Tap-opened cards ZERO bounce (damping 0.88–1.0); overshoot only for flick/throw/small accent. Bounce belongs to the OPEN, the close stays critically damped (~240 ms). Content crossfade 150–250 ms, content fade delayed 150 ms (shape first, text second).
- **Per-feature signatures (each different, from §9b/§4b — now mandatory, not optional):** Music = pill stretches horizontally first (scaleX overshoots while scaleY lags) + album art rotate −12°→0 spin-settle + scale 0.8→1 + progress draws in. Timer = digits roll (AnimatedContent vertical slide+fade per digit) + ring draws 0→360° red. Alert = bounce-in from top (spring 0.8/800) + glow pulse (shadow alpha 0→0.35→0 over ~600 ms). Search = liquid ripple (two staggered scale pulses 60 ms apart) + bar slides in after glass settles. Tools/Shelf = tiles stagger 40–60 ms, tiny pop (spring 0.6/800, scale 0.85→1 + fade). Idle→medium→full = three DISTINCT morphs.
- **Metaball / droplet merge-split:** ONE RenderEffect on the PARENT layer (chain blur ~16–24 px + colour-matrix alpha threshold ~50, constant ~−5000) — shapes split/merge like droplets, never crossfade. True field metaballs (Σ1/d² + marching squares) are CPU-bound — do NOT use.
- **Material Capsule lesson (50+ animations):** give EVERY event its own opening effect (charging, battery, timer, alert each animate in differently) — but only after the core morph is perfect.
- **Choreography:** tap squish 0.97 + haptic 0 ms → morph 380–460 ms → glass fade 180 ms (effects spring) → content stagger 200 ms → collapse 240 ms. Exit: content fades first (~80 ms), then shell shrinks into the pill. Swipe up = instant dismiss.
- **Performance (120 Hz, Snapdragon 732G, frame budget 8.3 ms):** graphicsLayer lambda only; never animate layout size; one updateTransition; blur radius static; shader area small; content at final width from the start; resize overlay window to island bounds where possible; R8 + Baseline Profile; redraw only on visible change; test on the real Redmi at 120 Hz.
- **Reference video:** dribbble-music-player-dynamic-island-animation.mp4 (attached) — study the music-player island animation frame by frame and copy its timing/feel.

