## 4. LYRICS — the exact truth + the offline fix (Alex: "lyrics wala bol raha h no lyrics but PixelMusic me to hoti h?")

The research verdict (verified against PixelMusic's own site FAQ + Android MediaMetadata docs + live LRCLIB query):
- **PixelMusic's lyrics do NOT come from the device, the file, or the MediaSession.** PixelMusic downloads them from **LRCLIB over the internet** and caches them in its own private database. Its YouTube Music streaming is audio only — no lyrics come from YouTube Music.
- **Android's MediaMetadata has NO lyrics key at all** (verified key list: TITLE, ARTIST, ALBUM, DURATION, artwork, etc. — never lyrics). There is no lyrics field in PlaybackState, notifications, or any documented PixelMusic provider/broadcast/extra. So the island can NEVER read lyrics from PixelMusic through the session — "No lyrics found on device" was technically true for a streamed track (no local file = no embedded lyrics), but the message is misleading and it must NOT show by default.
- **Implement now (offline first + LRCLIB online — Alex ALLOWED internet for lyrics only, Nov 25 ~22:27 IST):**
  1. Read lyrics for LOCAL files first: embedded USLT/SYLT tags + `.lrc` sidecar files via MediaStore. PixelMusic's own default source order is EMBEDDED_FIRST — match it.
  2. Synced lyrics line-by-line, scrolling in sync with playback position, exactly like PixelMusic — but ONLY when Alex taps the Lyrics button (Round 2 rule stands: never auto-show; default card shows controls only).
  3. Honest states, never the dead "No lyrics found on device" bar: if the track is streamed (no local file), show "Lyrics need internet — PixelMusic downloads them from LRCLIB" with a small "Learn more" line; if local but truly no lyrics, show "No lyrics for this track". The lyrics view must never appear uninvited.
  4. Timing offset setting (like PixelMusic) so Alex can fix lyrics that drift.
- **LRCLIB direct query — ENABLED (Alex allowed it, Nov 25 ~22:27 IST):** add the INTERNET permission and wire the client (GET https://lrclib.net/api/get?track_name=&artist_name=&album_name=&duration= — track+artist required, duration must match within ±2 s, 404 if no match; fallback /api/search; identifying User-Agent; ~45 req/min anonymous, ~90 identified; honour 429 Retry-After; parse syncedLyrics LRC; cache offline keyed by track; one request per track change). The network client MUST point at lrclib.net ONLY — no other host, ever — enforced in code (one base-URL constant, no generic HTTP client anywhere else in the app). Disclose it in Settings ("Lyrics download from LRCLIB (lrclib.net)") with a toggle "Lyrics from internet" default ON — turning it OFF kills all network use and the app behaves exactly as before (offline embedded/.lrc only). Live proof lyrics exist for his test track: LRCLIB returns full synced LRC for "Enemy" (Imagine Dragons).
- Full briefs: hidden_files/pixelmusic-lyrics-research-2026-11-25.md + hidden_files/browser-research-round3-2026-11-25.md §6.

## 5. SELECTION — PERMANENT fix, rebuild it (Alex: "select abhi bhi bekar h" — fourth report)

Screenshot 1000194417 (22:04, Reel) proves Round 2's fix did NOT land: two full-width blue bars, handles floating outside the text. Rebuild the selection path with this researched two-path architecture (full brief: hidden_files/ocr-selection-research-round3-2026-11-25.md):
- **Path A — delegate to the owning app (the ONLY way to get REAL native selection).** On long-press: fresh `getRootInActiveWindow()`, take the SMALLEST text node under the finger, and if `isTextSelectable || isEditable`, fire `ACTION_LONG_CLICK` (lets the app snap the word and draw its own handles/loupe) or `ACTION_SET_SELECTION` with word offsets from `refreshWithExtraData(EXTRA_DATA_TEXT_CHARACTER_LOCATION_KEY)` — the official per-character-location API. Draw NOTHING yourself. Read back `getTextSelectionStart/End` after `refresh()` and copy ONLY `text[start, end)`. Extend word-by-word via `ACTION_NEXT_AT_MOVEMENT_GRANULARITY` with `MOVEMENT_GRANULARITY_WORD`. ALWAYS check `performAction()`'s boolean — `false` means fall through to Path B.
- **Path B — freeze-frame OCR (Reels/video/images, where no text node exists).** Hide overlays → `takeScreenshot()` (API 30+, needs `canTakeScreenshot="true"`) → ML Kit v2 on the FROZEN bitmap → select whole `Element` words on the frozen frame, per-word translucent rects in AOSP blue `0x6633B5E5`, teardrop handles as SEPARATE small touchable overlay windows snapping to word edges, and the platform `Magnifier` (API 28+) attached to the frozen `ImageView` for a real loupe. Copy bar placed CLEAR of the selection, never over it.
- **Why the current build fails (7 independent causes — fix ALL of them):** (1) stale snapshot node bounds (docs warn nodes go stale — always re-fetch); (2) container-node hit test returning the full-screen Reel container (the blue wash — always take the SMALLEST node); (3) live-video drift (boxes cannot track 30 fps pixels — freeze is the only fix); (4) dp↔px density errors (~2.75x on this phone — convert exactly once, in one place); (5) five different coordinate spaces mixed (screen vs window vs view vs bitmap vs overlay — one mapping function, tested); (6) touch-interception dilemma (solved with a NON-touchable highlight layer + separate handle windows, exactly how `TextView.Editor` does it); (7) toolbar drawn over the selection (Copy bar goes below/clear, never on top).
- **Tests (build-gating):** pure-JVM tests for the word-hit/selection/copy/mapping model + Robolectric tests using `ShadowAccessibilityNodeInfo` (`setOnPerformActionListener`, `getPerformedActionsWithArgs`, `setRefreshReturnValue`) — including cases that FAIL the build if selection covers ≥80% of the screen or clipboard content contains unselected words. NOTE: Robolectric CANNOT test the real screenshot/OCR/Magnifier — those go on the phone checklist instead (test on a real Reel + a real photo + a real screenshot).
- Rules unchanged: screen reading OFF by default, OCR on-device only, reads ONLY the long-pressed text, nothing uploaded, no background clipboard reading.

