### 11a. Animation implementation (Compose ladder — use these exact APIs)
- Morph driver: `updateTransition` — one shared timeline, ALL properties (width, height, radius, position, scrim) from ONE scalar. `Animatable` for interrupt/velocity handling. `AnimatedContent` for digit rolls and state swaps. `SharedTransitionLayout` + `sharedElement` for the album-art hero morph (art grows from pill into the card). `anchoredDraggable` for in-pill swipes. Lookahead only if the camera dead zone needs holding during handover. Reference implementation: sinasamaki's "Made in Compose — Dynamic Island" (IslandState sealed class, shell via animateDpAsState spring StiffnessLow 200 / damping 0.6, content fadeIn(tween(300, delay 300)), bubble shake ±15 px + squish 1.5x→1x).
- Gooey/metaball: Route A (recommended) — ONE RenderEffect chain on the PARENT layer only: blur 16–24 px + ColorMatrix alpha row (alpha 50, constant −5000). Route B — AGSL RuntimeShader (API 33+, cutoff 0.5, entity blur ~30f). Route C (decorative blobs only) — Canvas radial gradients + BlendMode.Plus + Offscreen + withFrameNanos tick. Blur radius STATIC, shader area = island bounds only.
- Lottie: native springs for anything state-driven (morph, progress, visualizer, icon states); Lottie ONLY for decorative one-shots (success checkmark, unlock shimmer, empty states). Files MUST be bundled in res/raw or assets — URL sources forbidden. Total Lottie budget < 100 KB (lottie-compose 6.x.x, dotlottie-android 0.4.1).
- Animated vector drawables: play↔pause path morph (identical command counts/types per index — canonical 48 dp pathData), AnimatedStateListDrawable with reversible transitions, trimPath for ring/checkmark draw-on, heart pop spring 0.6/800. Visualizer is Canvas, NOT an AVD (3–5 bars, 80–120 ms phase stagger, drawBehind lambda).
- Exact M3E token table (verified against token files — do NOT use the wrong stiffness values floating around online; official stiffness ladder is 50/200/400/1500/10000): fast spatial 0.6/800 ~360–380 ms 9.5% overshoot; default spatial 0.8/380 ~435–460 ms 1.5%; slow spatial 0.8/200 ~600–620 ms 1.5%; fast effects 1.0/3800 ~150–170 ms 0%; default effects 1.0/1600 ~230–260 ms 0%; slow effects 1.0/800 ~330–350 ms 0%. Reduced-motion: spatial 0.9, stiffness 1400/700/300.
- Measured references: compact 36 pt → expanded 168 pt, radius 18→44 pt, damping 0.82 / response 0.38 s; transitions 400–500 ms; states 126x37 → 371x176.
- 120 Hz on Snapdragon 732G (8.33 ms budget): main-thread killers = recomposition churn (fix: defer state reads to offset{}/drawBehind{}/graphicsLayer{} lambdas), unstable params (Strong Skipping compares by === — a new list instance per emission = full recompose; fix @Immutable/ImmutableList). RenderThread killers = blur/shadow/overdraw/nested graphicsLayers (fix: one parent RenderEffect, static blur, small shader area, single cheap contact shadow). BIGGEST single win: resize the overlay window to island bounds (a full-screen transparent window forces full-screen compositing every frame). Measure with JankStats + Perfetto; R8 + Baseline Profile.

