### 11c. UI design rules (professional app UI — Settings / Wizard / Theme picker)
- **Settings: 7 grouped sections MAX.** M3 Expressive shaping — 28 dp outer corners, 4 dp inner, single item fully rounded; rows 56/72/88 dp; search bar on top; supporting text rewrites itself to say what the setting does NOW (status values live in the subtitle, e.g. "71% — about 21 hr left"); a switch acts at once, no confirm button.
- **Wizard: 5 steps MAX** — one priming card + one big button per permission (Accessibility → Notification → Overlay → Calibration → Done); per-permission state buttons (done = green COMPLETED, pending = TAP TO ENABLE); visible Skip on every screen; progress dots; ends on a LIVE island (first win, not an empty app). The system dialog is one-shot — a decline means <5% ever return via Settings, so prime properly first.
- **Theme picker:** 3 visual preview cards (Dark / Apple Glass / Liquid Glass) + 5 accent dots (ring + check when selected); glass for chrome only, never glass-on-glass.
- **Typography:** full M3 scale; pill text 13–15 sp semibold; nothing below 11 sp; sp always; sentence-case buttons.
- **Icons:** Material Symbols Rounded; 20 dp pill / 24 dp default / 40–48 dp hero; outline = idle, filled = active (the flip IS the state signal); opsz must match size — don't just scale a 24 dp icon down.
- **Dark mode — the split rule:** island pill pure black #000000 always (no shadow/border — anything else looks cheap on AMOLED); app surfaces on a #121212 grey ladder (0→16% white overlays by elevation); body text #E0E0E0, never pure white on pure black (21:1 halation, worst for astigmatism); contrast ≥4.5:1; desaturated accents; 150–200 ms transitions.
- **Motion-loop rule (from concept studies):** one shape, no cuts, content swaps with a quick blur, slight overshoot only, no bouncy easing/particles/glows/gradients on chrome. Heavy glass splits opinion — legibility first, always ship a solid fallback.
