## 12. Mascot — a little panda that peeks from the island (Alex saw it in other island apps, Nov 25 ~23:21 IST)

Alex saw dynamic island apps with a custom animation like a little panda peeking from the top, and wants it. Researched Nov 25: the app he almost certainly saw is **ORBI** (pixel pet inside a liquid-glass island — cat, dog, bunny, PANDA, fox, bear; the pet blinks, looks at the cursor, sleeps when idle, dances to music, reacts to clicks and notifications; its reel pet is named "Mochi"). The original is **Pixel Pals** (iOS, 2022 — a cat/dog sitting ON TOP of the pill, chasing a ball, sleeping, chilling). Same idea elsewhere: Chimomo (pet peeks out from the top of the screen), Pebbo (16 hand-drawn pets, 50+ animations), Mochi's Island (cat curls up in the island, naps, purrs), Pika! Spot (Android, tap-to-play character animations), iScreen Pet Island (corgis, cats, rabbits, panda), ApexNotch (MIT — pets run along the notch). **ORBI is proprietary — behavior reference ONLY, never copy its art or code. Draw an ORIGINAL panda.**
- **Five moves (the same in every app — build all five):** PERCH (sit on top of the pill), PEEK (pop up from behind the pill, look around, duck back — the exact move Alex described), RUN along the pill edge, DANCE to the music beat, SLEEP when idle (~30 s) and wake on notification/tap. Plus eyes following the finger, tap = jump + hearts, long-press = feed/play panel.
- **Implementation (researched, cheapest correct route): sprite-sheet frame animation on Compose Canvas.** One ORIGINAL 32x32 pixel panda drawn as part of this build (idle / blink / peek / dance / sleep / happy — about 18 frames total), cached bitmap, FilterQuality.None, withFrameNanos clock (idle 8 fps, dance 12 fps). Peek = translateY spring 0.8/380 from behind the pill. Cost: <100 KB APK, <1 ms/frame on the Snapdragon 732G. Lottie ONLY for 1–2 tiny one-shot reactions (dotLottie <20 KB — big Lottie JSON parses ~520 ms and renders 11–21 ms/frame, can drop frames). AVD cannot draw a character — do not use it for the mascot.
- **Rules:** toggleable in Settings ("Island pet" ON/OFF, default ON — Alex wants it, but it must be switchable); quiet hours (never animate 11 PM–7 AM unless the user opts in); the pet NEVER covers text or the camera; NEVER inside a music/alert card; pauses when the screen is off. Pet states: music playing = dance; timer done = happy jump; notification = peek + look; charging = sleep on the pill; low battery = sleepy eyes.
- **Mascot name:** call it "Mochi" in the UI (Alex's panda is Mochi — same spirit as the reference, original art).
